HST Office: Sheets cells that use HST functions can be saved as their results in .xlsx/.xls, the open document unchanged.

When a Sheets document whose cells use DOCSO, DOCTIEN, BODAU, TACHHO or TACHTEN is saved as .xlsx or
.xls, the bundled extension (org.hst.office.vi.SaveFormatCheck, hst-save-format-check.patch) may now
answer with named values instead of a boolean: Proceed, and ValueFunctions, the add-in functions whose
cells this one save writes as their current results. The save code registers that list for the
document only while the store runs (sfx2/hstsavevalues.hxx; cleared when the save ends, fails or is
cancelled), and the Excel cell table (shared by .xls and .xlsx) writes those cells as number, text or
boolean cells instead of formulas; an error result keeps its formula. Nothing in the open document
changes: no conversion, no undo step, no modified flag; URL, title and modified state after Save, Save
As and Save a Copy are those of a normal save. No copy of the document is made, so memory stays as for
a normal save. API saves, hidden documents and headless runs never ask and never convert.

